    "result_text": "The full test suite is green: **263 tests, 0 failures, 0 errors** (BUILD SUCCESS).\n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the tenure rule in `AssignMembershipLevel.java`, the step that assigns a new owner's `membershipLevel` during creation.\n\n**The change:** The pre-tenure factors (base 1, +1 for an email, +1 for `namesakeCount == 0`) are now explicitly capped at 3, and level 4 is unlocked only when tenure exceeds 365 days \u2014 computed as `ChronoUnit.DAYS.between(registrationDate, LocalDate.now()) > 365`.\n\n**Why a new owner never exceeds 3:** A newly created owner's `registrationDate` is the (business-day-adjusted) effective date, so its tenure is zero \u2014 well under the 365-day threshold \u2014 leaving the level at the pre-tenure cap of 3. The new acceptance test `coreNewOwnerCappedAtLevel3` (which maxes the pre-tenure factors: email present, no namesake) confirms the owner lands at level 3, not 4, and the audit log shows `membershipLevel=3` for the created owner.\n\nThe tenure factor is only additive on top of the capped pre-tenure level, so it never changes existing behavior for new owners \u2014 the rest of the suite stays green.",
